    529  f920							; there is no hot wall"). The PF is reflected, so the cell walk runs in
    530  f920							; MIRROR space (display col 39-c) — but the strip is an OBJECT drawn on ONE
    531  f920							; side only. A player at the MIRRORED column (display 37-38) therefore
    532  f920							; compared equal to a strip drawn at display 2-3, ~80 px away, and died on
    533  f920							; it. Require the player's PHYSICAL half to match the strip's side:
    534  f920							;   C from `cmp #80` = 1 when the player is on the RIGHT half;
    535  f920							;   MetaA b0	    = 1 when the strip is on the RIGHT half;
    536  f920							;   differing halves mean the overlap is the strip's MIRROR, not a touch.
