    931  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    932  fb32							; HcrClock — hcrunch animation clock (fixed full=10 since 2026-10-19).
    933  fb32							;   In:  X = full extent (cells, ≥1); reads EnemyRamP (StartFrame-pinned)
    934  fb32							;   Out: A = covered (1..full) — never 0 (always-solid stub)
    935  fb32							;   Clobbers A (X/Y preserved — unlike CrunchClock). No latch: the kill
    936  fb32							;   repeats on contact (DropArm respawns at the room top, so no loop).
    937  fb32							; s = EnemyRamP>>4 (0..15, one 256f period = 16 buckets of 16f):
    938  fb32							;   s 0-3   dwell at home  (eff 0)	  -> n=1, 64f stub
    939  fb32							;   s 4-12  grow to center  (eff s-3)	  -> n 2..full (1..9 cells of
    940  fb32							;	    8px — full=w>>1; w=20 record = center of the screen)
    941  fb32							;   s 13-15 fast retract    (eff 3*(15-s) = 6,3,0) — wipe home in 3
    942  fb32							;	    steps (the old instant far-end turn, stretched to center)
    943  fb32							; covered = 1 + min(eff, full-1). CrunchClock (sc>>2 triangle, ~4f/step)
    944  fb32							; stays for its VCR mirrors + verify_build token gate — only the two
    945  fb32							; hcrunch call sites moved here (16f/step, grow-to-center ruling
    946  fb32							; 2026-10-16). Both callers pass full=10 (PhHcrEntry stages it, HOV
    947  fb32							; tests it); the latch freeze was removed with the 2026-10-19 contract.
    948  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    949  fb32							; PARKED (user 2026-10-28: "HCrunch should stop (retracted) when it kills the player.
    950  fb32							; It keeps moving and killing him again and again", then "still restarts after a
    951  fb32							; while"). LoseLife arms Hover ($FF) and DropArm drops him back to the SAME spot while
    952  fb32							; this clock kept running, so the prefix was extended again on arrival. Two parks:
    953  fb32							;   * Hover set (any death in this room): held retracted until his first thrust;
    954  fb32							;   * EnemyDeadMask b7 = crunch SPENT: a hcrunch kill sets it (.HFkill) and it stays
    955  fb32							;     retracted for the rest of the visit - EnterRoom clears the mask, so the crunch
    956  fb32							;     cycles again the next time he enters the room (or after a game-over reload).
    957  fb32							; Parked = n=1 (clock pinned at 0); the kill test skips while parked too.
    958  fb32				   HcrClock
    959  fb32		       a5 ba		      lda	EnemyDeadMask
    960  fb34		       30 04		      bmi	.hcPark	; spent this visit
    961  fb36		       a5 9c		      lda	Hover
    962  fb38		       f0 07		      beq	.hcLive
    963  fb3a				   .hcPark
    964  fb3a		       a9 00		      lda	#0
    965  fb3c		       85 c2		      sta	EnemyRamP	; clock pinned: resumes at the home dwell
    966  fb3e		       a9 01		      lda	#1
    967  fb40		       60		      rts
    968  fb41				   .hcLive
    969  fb41		       e0 01		      cpx	#1
    970  fb43		       d0 03		      bne	.hcN
    971  fb45		       a9 01		      lda	#1	; full=1: n always 1
    972  fb47		       60		      rts
    973  fb48				   .hcN
    974  fb48		       a5 c2		      lda	EnemyRamP
    975  fb4a		       4a		      lsr
    976  fb4b		       4a		      lsr
    977  fb4c		       4a		      lsr
    978  fb4d		       4a		      lsr		; s = P>>4
    979  fb4e		       c9 04		      cmp	#4
    980  fb50		       b0 04		      bcs	.hcNd
    981  fb52		       a9 00		      lda	#0	; s0-3 dwell: eff 0
    982  fb54		       f0 11		      beq	.hcOut	; (always)
    983  fb56				   .hcNd
    984  fb56		       c9 0d		      cmp	#13
    985  fb58		       b0 05		      bcs	.hcNf
    986  fb5a		       38		      sec
    987  fb5b		       e9 03		      sbc	#3	; s4-12: eff = s-3 (1..9) — grow to center
    988  fb5d		       b0 08		      bcs	.hcOut	; (always, no borrow)
    989  fb5f				   .hcNf
