   1140  fd1e							; --- No ball in this room → BE the ball gate off. ---------------------
   1141  fd1e							; BandTab is the per-band ENABL gate for the cave (.Row). MetaA bit0 is
   1142  fd1e							; the band-0 gate AND (for a door) the "M1 strip on the RIGHT half"
   1143  fd1e							; flag — a door has no ball, so its bit0 must NOT enable one. Before
   1144  fd1e							; this, the door room rendered a wall-coloured (COLUPF) ball bar over
   1145  fd1e							; the band-0 opening: ENABL on, RESPBL never strobed (Temp=0) → the
   1146  fd1e							; ball free-ran at x72-79 (user screenshot 2026-10-17, door_right.png).
   1147  fd1e		       85 cf		      sta	BandTab
   1148  fd20		       85 d0		      sta	BandTab+1
   1149  fd22		       85 d1		      sta	BandTab+2
   1150  fd24		       85 d2		      sta	BandTab+3
   1151  fd26				   .SBTballDone
   1152  fd26							; --- strip destroyed by a bomb? (EnemyDeadMask b3 — StripBlastCheck
   1153  fd26							; set it this overscan) → blank all band gates so the cave renders no
   1154  fd26							; strip AND clear BallX (Temp): the pack below keys off Temp, so a dead
   1155  fd26							; strip emits no ball column/gates and every overlay stays transparent.
   1156  fd26							; (2026-10-25, user level 7 room 1: only BandTab was blanked, the pack
   1157  fd26							; kept the column nibble — the strip vanished but still blocked.)
   1158  fd26							; BandTab restages from ROM next room entry. ---
   1159  fd26		       a5 ba		      lda	EnemyDeadMask
   1160  fd28		       29 08		      and	#$08
   1161  fd2a		       f0 0c		      beq	.SBTstripAlive
   1162  fd2c		       a9 00		      lda	#0
